+To examine their complementarity, we further run \griffin{} with the union of the SmartFuzz and \tool{} seeds, which covers 413,021 branches in total (73,315, 48,030, 132,077, and 159,599 branches on MonetDB, Virtuoso, DuckDB, and ClickHouse, respectively) and detects 35 bugs in total, i.e., 13 and 18 more bugs than \tool{} alone and SmartFuzz alone, respectively. The combination detects more bugs than either seed source alone on all four DBMSs, and achieves higher coverage on Virtuoso and ClickHouse. On MonetDB and DuckDB, its coverage is lower than that of \tool{} alone, and it executes 38.5\% and 22.4\% fewer test cases than SmartFuzz alone within 24 hours, respectively. The additional seeds reduce the execution throughput, leaving fewer mutation opportunities for potentially more valuable seeds.
 
